<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:23Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Americans voted against Trump's Iran war. Gulf countries hope that means an end to the conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:305d339082dbe20b20005464334c2f54109663bd79631dff91f850428cf56d07</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T19:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/americans-voted-against-trump-s-iran-war-gulf-countries-hope-that-means-an-end-to-the-conflict/a-79868398--8084b702dfa9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/americans-voted-against-trump-s-iran-war-gulf-countries-hope-that-means-an-end-to-the-conflict/a-79868398?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US midterm results showed how unpopular Donald Trump's Iran war is. Now, Gulf countries, trapped for months in the middle of the war between the US and Iran, see reason for optimism.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Arrests and investigations as Serbia begins post-election clean-up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63fd23b570eae75bcdee6e0519f72c3c2ea015a35486fa0654a98607142f64ab</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T17:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/arrests-and-investigations-as-serbia-begins-post-election-clean-up/a-79868652--133f253d322e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/arrests-and-investigations-as-serbia-begins-post-election-clean-up/a-79868652?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The landslide victory of the Students' List in Serbia's general election seems to have removed a blockage in the justice system: Cases that were long stalled are now suddenly moving forward.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran signals satisfaction, skepticism after US midterm vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5556dff3f9d34f7fe8dc0dc05a0a69407a3e1a6d09d5f637d933f56961048db8</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-signals-satisfaction-skepticism-after-us-midterm-vote/a-79867149--f14e22022dc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-signals-satisfaction-skepticism-after-us-midterm-vote/a-79867149?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the Iranian regime says the US midterms will not change Washington's policy toward Tehran, some officials and commentators see the resounding Democratic victory as blowback against the Iran war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What does Trump's midterm elections loss mean for strained US-India ties?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9c03ebcc1c005e32444b9bff7219cfaf84245b0c138656eafcbc4a0814d34d3</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T13:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-does-trump-s-midterm-elections-loss-mean-for-strained-us-india-ties/a-79865777--7836c1679b1c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-does-trump-s-midterm-elections-loss-mean-for-strained-us-india-ties/a-79865777?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's electoral setback might give New Delhi and Washington space to reset relations, but there is no guarantee that the US will actually change its approach to India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea tells EU to 'mind its own business' on human rights</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d614cfeec773785b1856efe3c898df88316ba96ac63924c3244030a115da5430</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-tells-eu-to-mind-its-own-business-on-human-rights/a-79862196--b096a2c3122f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-tells-eu-to-mind-its-own-business-on-human-rights/a-79862196?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea's UN mission has lashed out at the European Union over a draft UN resolution. Pyongyang has said the West does not have a monopoly on human rights.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bomb threats disrupt several flights across Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fe3a619e4a2dde23fcdaf26753d0dec4dbae19eaf5a6514c29102d4ac546039</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:03:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T10:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bomb-threats-disrupt-several-flights-across-europe/a-79861216--3a3ce6d11c4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bomb-threats-disrupt-several-flights-across-europe/a-79861216?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least a dozen flights were either diverted or landed with a military escort after bomb or security threats. The first reported case involved a flight from Dublin to Rome landing outside Paris and more soon followed.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea tests Arctic shipping route amid Russia-West row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96586c7d7d54ca8b808f8f6cd72ae3500a2c3452a803eebc5113303f3e5cd5e0</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907--d831b46c670a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For South Korean ships, navigating off the north coast of Russia dramatically reduces travel time to Europe, but the pro-Ukraine coalition might see it as undermining their efforts to isolate Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What the Democrats' midterms win means for the US economy and Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5640416cff9f93bcd577b722d2e4e67bb0b366a4c0fb6787979a88bfcde57d84</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T07:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716--124f824b0e07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From high oil prices and data centers to tariffs and mounting debt, economic concerns played a key role in the crushing defeat of President Donald Trump's Republicans. So can the Democrats now make a difference?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Winners, losers, the EU: Five takeaways from the US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d865116738006cec3dde0a29e8b055821a264208acd9b8dcec1a6a524a8d84e9</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T20:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/winners-losers-the-eu-five-takeaways-from-the-us-midterms/a-79858901--d5d91689d3d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/winners-losers-the-eu-five-takeaways-from-the-us-midterms/a-79858901?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's Republicans suffered a crushing defeat in Tuesday's midterm elections, with the Democrats wresting control of Congress. What does this mean for US politics and the world?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>36 years later: Hungary opens Communist-era secret service files</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e8a785a7231840003eb7e8e0bc595db2b3ddf809687bb38690cf5aae3ba2d81</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T19:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/36-years-later-hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-service-files/a-79858016--dc09772faa12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/36-years-later-hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-service-files/a-79858016?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Decades after the end of Soviet rule, Hungary is releasing all its secret service files. The disclosure is sparking fresh debate about informants, guilt and responsibility.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kosovo: Outrage as authorities accused of not helping femicide victim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f31df5d13fac73cbe5f0a4c4efedc4c63dcabed0f051665f845d29576a3cefd</id><updated>2026-11-06T07:01:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kosovo-outrage-as-authorities-accused-of-not-helping-femicide-victim/a-79856726--34859fc77a44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kosovo-outrage-as-authorities-accused-of-not-helping-femicide-victim/a-79856726?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite reporting her husband to the police and pleading for protection, Arlinda Zekaj was brutally murdered. Now, thousands in Kosovo are protesting what they say is a dramatic failure of state institutions.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
